        "original_id": "cf5c068e-404b-523a-b277-f733dd2134db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Eucommia, Maytenus\n- Taxonomy: genera, Celastraceae\n- Places: China, Central and South America, Southeast Asia, Micronesia, Australasia, the Indian Ocean, Africa\n- Concepts: fossil record, native distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Eucommia is a genus of small trees now native to China.\n- Eucommia has a fossil record that indicates it once had a much wider distribution.\n- Maytenus is a genus of flowering plants in the staff vine family Celastraceae.\n- Members of the genus Maytenus are distributed throughout Central and South America, Southeast Asia, Micronesia, Australasia, the Indian Ocean, and Africa.",
